<script server>
// Is the visitor signed in? Read once here so SiteNav, SiteFooter and every
// page's CTA agree, on all 23 marketing pages.
//
// This replaced a bare <script> in index.stx that queried [data-auth-login],
// [data-auth-signup] and [data-auth-cta] and rewrote their text and href. Two
// things were wrong with it: the hooks it targeted live in SiteNav and
// SiteFooter — shared by every marketing page — while the script itself was on
// the home page only, so a signed-in visitor saw "Log in / Sign up" everywhere
// except "/"; and rewriting after paint meant a visible flicker.
//
// Server-side is safe here specifically because these responses are not
// cacheable: every one sets Cache-Control: no-store and a per-visitor
// X-CSRF-Token cookie, and the CDN in config/cloud.ts is disabled. If HTML
// caching is ever introduced, this must move behind a Vary: Cookie or go back
// to the client — auth state baked into a shared cache entry leaks across
// visitors.
//
// Client-side was the alternative and costs more than it looks: marketing pages
// currently load router.js only, not runtime.js (measured), so a <script client>
// here would pull the whole signals runtime onto all 23 public pages to decide
// the wording of two links.
let signedIn = false
try {
  signedIn = !!(typeof requestContext !== 'undefined' && requestContext.cookie && requestContext.cookie('bughq_token'))
}
catch {
  signedIn = false
}
</script>

<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1">
    {{-- No <title> or description here on purpose. Both are owned by each page's
         useSeoMeta() call, which also derives og:* and twitter:* from the same
         two strings so they cannot drift apart.

         Hardcoding them here actively breaks that: @yield renders an EMPTY tag
         when a page supplies no section, and injectSeo skips any tag already
         declared — so `<meta name="description" content="">` shipped on every
         page that had no @section('description'), suppressing the real one.
         Emitting nothing lets useSeoMeta be the single source. --}}
    {{-- The font links and the pre-paint theme guard are deliberately NOT here.
         They live in config/ui.ts `app.head` (Stage 1), and injectConfigHeadTags
         adds them to this head, deduped on href and on inline script content.
         Re-adding them would emit a second copy on every marketing page.

         /marketing.css does stay here rather than in the global head: it defines
         :root, html, body, * and a, plus .btn / .panel / .mono / .reveal, which
         the authenticated app pages also use. Globalising it would restyle the
         app. Scoping it to this layout is what makes it safe. --}}
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="/marketing.css">
    @stack('styles')
  </head>
  <body>
    @include('SiteNav')
    @yield('content')
    @include('SiteFooter')
    @stack('scripts')
  </body>
</html>
